Preserve spatial control from exploration observations to operating geometry (@mine-survey: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/USBR-Engineering-Geology-Field-Manual.lingua#r_5WS5PNK19008B3SV6D1WWNVTRE", #source "../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA", #source "../sources/Surface-Mining-Technology-NPTEL.lingua#r_5J36XSV6KZRNWX3J51Q4TRV7KG", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "../../../inquiry/metrology/foundations/Sampling-and-representativeness.lingua#r_0F0VEC42GPQPRZM0S7MXF7GAEH") { r_1ZDJAQC4S016X5KHEY4RK8GKBE
**Read:** [Engineering Geology Field Manual — U.S. Bureau of Reclamation](../sources/USBR-Engineering-Geology-Field-Manual.lingua#r_5WS5PNK19008B3SV6D1WWNVTRE), volume I mapping/documentation and volume II survey/core-handling methods in full; [Hard Rock Miner’s Handbook — Jack de la Vergne, fifth edition](../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA), the complete mine layout and survey-related sections; [Surface Mining Technology — Kaushik Dey, NPTEL](../sources/Surface-Mining-Technology-NPTEL.lingua#r_5J36XSV6KZRNWX3J51Q4TRV7KG), the full relevant geometry/layout lectures.

Mine geometry depends on a defined spatial reference, survey control, instrument/method, uncertainty, and updates as workings change. Surface and underground coordinates, elevations, orientation references, and historical plans must be reconciled before combining observations or evaluating clearances and volumes.

Survey precision, reference accuracy, interpolation, map generalization, and geological uncertainty are separate. A dense digital point cloud or a highly zoomed model cannot repair an incorrect datum, unmeasured hidden surface, or misidentified contact. Preserve control and transformation information.

Mine plans connect observed workings, geological interpretations, equipment routes, utilities, ground conditions, and operating boundaries. A planned excavation and an as-built/surveyed excavation can differ. Record what was measured, inferred, approved for a particular purpose, or superseded.

**Work:** reconstruct a published teaching survey/plan with explicit units, datums, control, and uncertainty. Independently check a distance, gradient, volume, or coordinate transformation. Compare a planned and observed geometry and explain what new observations would resolve a consequential mismatch.

Read the full field/manual survey and documentation sections and the mine-layout course material. Practical surveying requires actual suitable instrument work; a document/CAD reconstruction demonstrates a different scope. Continue through [A specimen, a sampling target, and a result about a population](../../../inquiry/metrology/foundations/Sampling-and-representativeness.lingua#r_0F0VEC42GPQPRZM0S7MXF7GAEH) for shared sampling reasoning before defining a mine-specific sampling programme.

**Continue:** [A specimen, a sampling target, and a result about a population](../../../inquiry/metrology/foundations/Sampling-and-representativeness.lingua#r_0F0VEC42GPQPRZM0S7MXF7GAEH).

